    "developerBrief": "## Bug: Pending badge count mismatch (stuck at 1, empty queue) + private note requires public note\n\n### What was reported\n- Reporter (PoS Desk / tech 1005) sees the Pending tab badge show \"(1)\" while the call list under that filter shows \"No matches for the current filters — try clearing the funnel.\"\n- Confirmed: badge stuck at 1 after refresh, after Clear all filters + reselecting filter, and after switching Technician filter to All/other users (still doesn't resolve — reporter says switching technician filter doesn't change the stuck appearance, implying the counter itself may be global/cached rather than scoped per filter).\n- Separately, reporter also states: \"Unable to leave a private note without leaving a public note. not all calls require a public note.\" — appears to be a second complaint about the notes feature in the call detail pane, where adding a private note forces a public note to also be added.\n\n### Where it likely lives\n- Section: review (Review queue)\n- Files: `src/server.js` (routes `GET /api/reviews`, `PATCH /api/reviews/:id/notes`), `src/store.js` (review store / pending count logic)\n- Frontend: `public/index.html` (Pending tab badge rendering, filter panel, notes box in detail pane)\n\n### Reproduction (as understood, some assumed)\n1. Navigate to Review > Pending tab.\n2. Filter by Technician = POS Desk (or no filter — unclear, see assumption).\n3. Badge shows \"(1)\" but call list is empty regardless of filter state.\n4. Separately: open a call detail pane, attempt to add a private-only note without a public note — UI/backend blocks or forces a public note to be entered too.\n\n### Ranked hypotheses\n1. (medium) Badge counter and list query use different filter/eligibility logic — e.g. counter tallies all pending regardless of some exclusion the list applies (status flag, missing required field, soft-deleted record).\n2. (medium) A specific call record in `./data` is corrupted/orphaned (e.g. missing technician or client reference) so it's excluded from `GET /api/reviews` results but still counted by whatever increments the pending badge.\n3. (high) Notes feature: `PATCH /api/reviews/:id/notes` or the Halo posting logic (`src/halo.js`) treats private and public notes as a single required pair rather than independent optional fields — needs code-level check to confirm whether this is a UI gate or backend validation.\n\n### Suggested approach\n1. Inspect how the Pending badge count is computed (likely a separate lightweight count query or cached value in `store.js`) vs. how `GET /api/reviews` filters results — diff the eligibility conditions.\n2. Search `./data` for pending-state call records with technician field matching POS Desk/1005 that might be malformed or missing fields causing them to be silently excluded from the list query.\n3. Check system/user-action logs (per `/api/reviews/:id/history` audit trail mechanism) for the call to see if it was completed/merged but not properly decremented from the pending counter.\n4. For the notes issue, inspect the notes UI logic and `/notes` PATCH handler and `src/halo.js` to see if public note is required to accompany a private note; confirm whether this is intentional design or a bug, and if a bug, decouple the two fields so each can be submitted independently.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Pending badge count always matches the number of calls actually shown in the corresponding filtered list (or the discrepancy is in a documented global vs filtered scope — clarify via code).\n- A stuck/orphaned call does not show in a count without being reachable in the list; add handling/logging if a record is excluded, so counts stay consistent.\n- User can add a private-only note to a call without being forced to also add a public note (unless this is confirmed-intentional Halo API constraint, in which case surface that clearly in the UI with explanation).\n\n### Unverified assumptions\n- Whether the badge count is meant to be scoped to the active filters (e.g. updates with Technician dropdown) or global; screenshot shows filter panel with Technician = POS Desk (1) and funnel badge \"1\" which may just reflect '1 active filter', not pending call count — needs clarification from reporter/admin whether that \"(1)\" badge is the filter-count badge or a separate pending-call badge (ambiguous from screenshot alone).\n- Whether the notes complaint pertains to the same call session or is a general/unrelated feature complaint appended to this report.\n- Reporter could not confirm (via Network tab/logs) whether the underlying call record exists server-side — backend state unverified.",
